= Khinchuk Goes Over

Lev Khinchuk, the former chairman of the Moscow Soviet's executive, has accepted a post in the Soviet government's cooperative administration. He will serve it, in later years, as ambassador to Berlin and to London. The cooperatives that he led have lost their patron, and our party its best contact among the Moscow businessmen.
